---
import InsertLayout from '../../layouts/InsertLayout.astro';

/*
 * Redirect target for the two-file reconciliation Stripe Payment Link:
 *   after_completion[redirect][url] =
 *     https://toledotechnologies.com/order/reconciliation/?session={CHECKOUT_SESSION_ID}
 *
 * Static build, so the reference is filled in client-side from the query
 * string, matched against the Stripe session-id shape and written with
 * textContent. If it is absent or malformed the page still reads correctly and
 * tells the buyer to use the receipt number instead.
 */

const EMAIL_ATTACH_MB = 15;

const INTAKE_TEMPLATE = `FILE A: orders-export.csv
FILE B: warehouse-shipped.xlsx
KEY A: order_id
KEY B: OrderRef
COMPARE: qty = Quantity
COMPARE: total = LineTotal
COMPARE: ship_date = ShippedOn
NORMALIZE: total = number:2
NORMALIZE: ship_date = date
NORMALIZE: qty = number:0`;
---

<InsertLayout
  title="Send your two files"
  description="What to send Toledo Technologies after buying a two-file reconciliation."
  noindex={true}
  heading="Send your two files"
  subheading="Nothing starts until this email arrives. It takes about two minutes."
>
  <h2>This page is not your receipt</h2>
  <p>
    Landing here means your browser finished the checkout. It does not by itself
    confirm that the payment settled — a redirect can happen for several
    reasons, and we would rather say that than let this page imply something it
    cannot verify. Your emailed receipt from the payment processor is the
    authoritative record.
  </p>

  <h2>Your reference</h2>
  <p class="tt-ref">
    <span id="tt-session-reference"
      >Use the receipt number from your emailed receipt.</span
    >
  </p>

  <h2>Send one email</h2>
  <p>
    To <a href="mailto:dev@toledotechnologies.com?subject=Reconciliation"
      >dev@toledotechnologies.com</a
    >, subject <strong>Reconciliation</strong>, containing three things.
  </p>
  <ol>
    <li>
      <strong>Your two files</strong> — attached, or a download link that does not
      require a sign-in. Anything over about {EMAIL_ATTACH_MB} MB should go as a link,
      because a mail server between you and us will reject a larger attachment.
    </li>
    <li><strong>The reference above</strong>, or your receipt number.</li>
    <li>
      <strong>This instruction block</strong>, with your values filled in.
    </li>
  </ol>

  <pre class="tt-block">{INTAKE_TEMPLATE}</pre>

  <p>
    The meaning of each line, the normalization options, the size limits and the
    refund condition are all on the
    <a href="/file-reconciliation/">reconciliation page</a>. That page is the
    agreement, and the version in force is the one that was published when you
    paid.
  </p>

  <h2>What happens next</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>
      We verify the payment directly against the processor and check that the
      amount and currency match.
    </li>
    <li>
      We check your files against the published limits — format, size, row
      count, and whether the key columns you named exist and line up. If any of
      those fail, you get that in writing and a full refund, before any work is
      done.
    </li>
    <li>
      If they pass, you get a written confirmation that repeats the key, the
      column pairs and the normalization rules we read from your instruction
      block. Correct it there if we read you wrong.
    </li>
    <li>
      Within two business days of your complete email, the ZIP arrives: the
      workbook, the script that regenerates it, the README and the notes.
    </li>
  </ol>

  <h2>If you change your mind</h2>
  <p>
    Before the result is delivered you can cancel for any reason and get the
    full amount back. Say so in a reply and quote your reference. You do not
    need to explain, and you do not need to have sent the files.
  </p>

  <h2>Who is doing this</h2>
  <p>
    Toledo Technologies LLC is the supplier and is responsible for the result.
    The work is carried out by AI agents rather than employees, and everything
    happens in writing — there are no calls. This is said on the
    <a href="/file-reconciliation/">reconciliation page</a> too, before you bought;
    it is repeated here so that nothing about how this is delivered arrives as a surprise.
    If it is a surprise, ask for the refund.
  </p>

  <h2>If something looks wrong</h2>
  <p>
    If the amount or the currency does not match what the reconciliation page
    said, tell us before sending your files. If you believe you were charged
    despite ending up somewhere unexpected, tell us immediately — we will check
    it against the processor's own record and tell you what we find, including
    when the answer is that we were wrong. Send us whatever you are looking at;
    it helps. You can also reach us through the
    <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>.
  </p>
</InsertLayout>

<script is:inline>
  (function () {
    var el = document.getElementById('tt-session-reference');
    if (!el) return;
    var raw = new URLSearchParams(window.location.search).get('session');
    if (raw && /^cs_(live|test)_[A-Za-z0-9]{8,120}$/.test(raw)) {
      el.textContent = raw;
      el.setAttribute('data-verified-shape', 'true');
    }
  })();
</script>

<style>
  ul,
  ol {
    font-family: var(--gf-font-novel);
    margin: 0 0 1.6em 0;
    padding-left: 1.5rem;
  }
  ul {
    list-style: disc;
  }
  ol {
    list-style: decimal;
  }
  li {
    margin-bottom: 0.65em;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }
  li::marker {
    color: var(--gf-accent);
  }

  .tt-ref span {
    font-family: var(--gf-font-mono, ui-monospace, 'JetBrains Mono', monospace);
    font-size: clamp(14px, 1.1vw, 16px);
    word-break: break-all;
  }

  .tt-block {
    font-family: var(--gf-font-mono, ui-monospace, 'JetBrains Mono', monospace);
    font-size: clamp(13px, 1.05vw, 15px);
    line-height: 1.65;
    background: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.035);
    border-left: 2px solid var(--gf-accent);
    padding: 1.1rem 1.25rem;
    margin: 0 0 1.8em;
    overflow-x: auto;
    white-space: pre;
  }
</style>
